class.description:
A [PckPackage] holds the file list of a pack. It has two forms:
- An [b]opened pack[/b] is read from a [code].pck[/code] file by [method PckPackageServer.open] or by [code]load("res://dlc.pck")[/code]. Only the header and the directory are read, and the pack is never mounted (see [method PckPackageServer.mount]). [member pack_path] is the pack file.
- A [b]pack description[/b] is created with [code]PckPackage.new()[/code] or loaded from a [code].tres[/code] or [code].res[/code] file. It maps target paths to sources: files on disk ([method add_file]), data in memory ([method add_file_from_buffer]) or files of the [member base_pack]. Saved as [code].tres[/code], it is plain text that can be versioned. [method is_description] returns [code]true[/code].
Files can be added, removed and renamed in memory in both forms. [method PckPackageServer.build] writes the result as a new pack, and so does [code]ResourceSaver.save(package, "user://patch.pck")[/code]. Reading file data and verifying go through [PckPackageServer].
A description stores [member base_pack], [member alignment], [member encrypted_directory] and two storage-only properties: [code]files[/code], an [Array] of [Dictionary] with the keys [code skip-lint]path[/code] and one of [code]source[/code] (a file path), [code]data[/code] (a [PackedByteArray]) or [code]from_pack[/code] (a path in [member base_pack]), plus [code]encrypt[/code] if the file is encrypted; and [code]removals[/code], a [PackedStringArray] of removal entries. An opened pack saved as [code].tres[/code] becomes a description whose files come from the pack. The key set with [method set_key] is never stored.
Paths inside a package can be given with or without [code]res://[/code]; they are always listed with [code]res://[/code].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# Open a pack, edit it and build a new one.
var package: PckPackage = load("res://dlc/level_pack.pck")
package.add_file_from_buffer("res://levels/extra.txt", "Hello".to_utf8_buffer())
package.remove_file("res://levels/old.tscn")
ResourceSaver.save(package, "user://mods/level_pack_v2.pck")

# Describe a pack as text and build it later.
var description := PckPackage.new()
description.add_file("res://textures/a.png", "res://art/a.png")
ResourceSaver.save(description, "res://packs/textures.tres")
ResourceSaver.save(description, "user://textures.pck")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// Open a pack, edit it and build a new one.
var package = GD.Load<PckPackage>("res://dlc/level_pack.pck");
package.AddFileFromBuffer("res://levels/extra.txt", "Hello".ToUtf8Buffer());
package.RemoveFile("res://levels/old.tscn");
ResourceSaver.Save(package, "user://mods/level_pack_v2.pck");

// Describe a pack as text and build it later.
var description = new PckPackage();
description.AddFile("res://textures/a.png", "res://art/a.png");
ResourceSaver.Save(description, "res://packs/textures.tres");
ResourceSaver.Save(description, "user://textures.pck");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Loaded packs are cached by path like every resource: a second [code]load()[/code] returns the same object. Use [method PckPackageServer.open] for a fresh object, or [constant ResourceLoader.CACHE_MODE_REPLACE] to read a changed pack into the cached object.
[b]Note:[/b] A [PckPackage] is not thread-safe. Use one package from one thread at a time.
